# Cloudflare Pages cache rules.
#
# The problem this solves: HTML pages carry versioned asset links like
# js/admin.js?v=11. If the HTML itself is cached in a visitor's browser for
# hours, they never see the new version string, so they keep running old
# JavaScript long after a deploy. Admins and clients then report that a fix
# "didn't work" when the fix is already live on the server.
#
# Rule: HTML always revalidates (cheap - a 304 when nothing changed).
# Versioned CSS/JS can cache hard, because the ?v= bump forces a new URL.

/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

/css/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

/js/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

/portal/css/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

/portal/js/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000
